WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.834
"This way!" Brody shouted. He grabbed Julia, who seemed to be frozen with terror, and yanked her into motion.

2
00:00:11.835 --> 00:00:17.718
Markos was already sprinting ahead of them, away from the charging metal bull.

3
00:00:17.719 --> 00:00:22.981
"What is that thing?" Julia cried as she ran alongside Brody.

4
00:00:22.982 --> 00:00:28.099
"The bull is made of metal, but it acts like it's alive! That's so weird!"

5
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:34.484
Brody shot her a surprised look. " Now you think things are weird?" he

6
00:00:34.485 --> 00:00:40.397
said. "You didn't seem to think it was weird to ride in a flying chariot. Or to travel back in time

7
00:00:40.398 --> 00:00:47.741
either." "Please," Markos called over his shoulder. "There is no time for talking right

8
00:00:47.742 --> 00:00:53.343
now!" Brody saw that the sheer rock wall continued to their right for as far as he could

9
00:00:53.344 --> 00:00:59.064
see. So did the thorny thicket on their left. Just ahead he spotted a

10
00:00:59.065 --> 00:01:04.821
forest. "Keep going," Brody said. "Maybe the bull can't fit between the tree

11
00:01:04.822 --> 00:01:10.204
trunks." Brody was right—sort of. The metal bull was still charging after

12
00:01:10.205 --> 00:01:17.676
them. But when the kids darted into the forest, the bull halted, roaring with

13
00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:23.643
fury. "Clever strategy, Brody!" Markos cried breathlessly. "We stopped

14
00:01:23.644 --> 00:01:29.180
him." Julia gasped. "No, we didn't—keep

15
00:01:29.181 --> 00:01:32.844
running!" The bull was already ramming its way

16
00:01:32.845 --> 00:01:36.618
forward. Tree trunks cracked and fell in every

17
00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:41.342
direction. Soon the kids found themselves running out of the far end of the

18
00:01:41.343 --> 00:01:48.275
forest. Once again they were trapped in an open area between the high rock wall and the thorny

19
00:01:48.276 --> 00:01:53.732
thicket. "What are we going to do?" Julia glanced over her shoulder at the

20
00:01:53.733 --> 00:01:57.973
bull. "Run faster!" Brody yelled

21
00:01:57.974 --> 00:02:03.747
back. "Easy for you to say, champion," Markos grumbled

22
00:02:03.748 --> 00:02:09.755
breathlessly. Brody didn't answer. He'd just spotted something ahead.

23
00:02:09.756 --> 00:02:15.396
"Uh-oh." The others looked ahead too. "Oh no!" Julia

24
00:02:15.397 --> 00:02:22.745
cried. A short distance from them, the rock wall curved out, blocking their way

25
00:02:22.746 --> 00:02:27.240
completely! "What are we going to do?" Julia cried

26
00:02:27.241 --> 00:02:34.579
again. "We'll have to try going back through the thicket," Markos said. "Perhaps that will slow the

27
00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:40.057
bull." "That won't work," Brody pointed out. "That metal bull won't feel any

28
00:02:40.058 --> 00:02:42.977
scratches. It will charge through faster than we can

29
00:02:42.978 --> 00:02:46.486
go." They reached the rock wall and skidded to a

30
00:02:46.487 --> 00:02:52.969
stop. Julia stared up at the sheer cliff. "What other choice do we have?" she

31
00:02:52.970 --> 00:03:01.531
said. Brody glanced at the bull, which was still coming at them. "I don't know," he said, feeling

32
00:03:01.532 --> 00:03:07.366
frantic. The cliff didn't have a single handhold that he could see—they couldn't climb to safety that way.

33
00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:11.874
He looked around for a sturdy branch or anything else he could use as a weapon.

34
00:03:11.875 --> 00:03:18.208
Maybe he could fight off the bull long enough for Julia and Markos to crawl through the thicket to safety.

35
00:03:18.209 --> 00:03:24.506
"Hello down there!" a voice called from overhead. "Look up! I'm throwing you a rope!"

36
00:03:24.507 --> 00:03:33.026
Brody gasped and looked up. A face was peering down at them. It was Heracles!

37
00:03:33.027 --> 00:03:38.721
"Hurry!" Another face appeared beside Heracles—his brother, Iphicles.

38
00:03:38.722 --> 00:03:42.086
"The bull automaton will reach you in a moment!"

39
00:03:42.087 --> 00:03:47.665
A thick rope dropped down near them. Heracles was holding the other end.

40
00:03:47.666 --> 00:03:52.319
"Grab hold of it," Heracles called. "Now!"

41
00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:59.207
"All of us?" Markos looked worried. "But how can you . . . you can't possibly—"

42
00:03:59.208 --> 00:04:04.603
"Hurry!" Iphicles yelled. "It's coming!"

43
00:04:04.604 --> 00:04:09.064
He was right. The bull was charging toward them.

44
00:04:09.065 --> 00:04:13.486
"Oh well," Brody said. "Here goes nothing."

45
00:04:13.487 --> 00:04:18.324
He grabbed the rope with both hands. So did Julia and Markos.

46
00:04:18.325 --> 00:04:21.490
"We're ready!" Markos called.

47
00:04:21.491 --> 00:04:26.098
"They can't do this, can they?" Julia's voice was shaking.

48
00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:32.097
"They can't possibly lift all three of us at once. Not all the way up that cliff!"

49
00:04:32.098 --> 00:04:38.763
"Heracles lifted that wagon by himself," Brody reminded her. He tried to sound confident.

50
00:04:38.764 --> 00:04:43.080
But inside he was just as scared as Julia looked.

51
00:04:43.081 --> 00:04:49.502
What if Heracles dropped them when they were halfway up that cliff? They could all be killed!

52
00:04:49.503 --> 00:04:54.881
Then Brody would never get to be in the Olympic Games. He'd never return home.

53
00:04:54.882 --> 00:04:59.205
He'd never play football again, or see his parents, or . . .

54
00:04:59.206 --> 00:05:04.963
Brody was so busy worrying, he almost didn't notice when his feet left the ground.

55
00:05:04.964 --> 00:05:09.170
He snapped back to reality when Markos shouted in his ear.

56
00:05:09.171 --> 00:05:15.263
"Hurry!" Markos yelled, sounding terrified. "It's almost here!"

57
00:05:15.264 --> 00:05:20.455
"Brody," Julia said. "Lift your feet! Quick!"

58
00:05:20.456 --> 00:05:25.963
Brody did as she said. He felt something swish past under one sandal.

59
00:05:25.964 --> 00:05:32.382
When he looked down, he gulped as he realized it was one of the bull's sharp metal horns.

60
00:05:32.383 --> 00:05:44.098
Up above he could hear Heracles grunting with effort as he slowly, slowly pulled them up.

61
00:05:44.099 --> 00:05:49.521
Finally Brody and the others were safe at the top of the cliff.

62
00:05:49.522 --> 00:05:57.983
"Thanks, dude!" Brody said to Heracles. "Hera and Hephaestus tried to kill us with that bull statue!"

63
00:05:57.984 --> 00:06:01.465
"It's an automaton—that's an animated statue.

64
00:06:01.466 --> 00:06:09.704
Hephaestus frequently creates them." Iphicles peered down at the bull.

65
00:06:09.705 --> 00:06:12.749
"We should get away from here," he added.

66
00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:18.163
"If the automaton returns to Hera and Hephaestus, they could come looking for us."

67
00:06:18.164 --> 00:06:22.557
"Good thinking, brother." Heracles smiled at the others.

68
00:06:22.558 --> 00:06:26.340
"Are you strong enough to walk, or should I carry you?"

69
00:06:26.341 --> 00:06:34.882
Brody blinked. Heracles might be even stronger than Brody had realized, but that didn't mean Brody was a wimp!

70
00:06:34.883 --> 00:06:39.424
"No, we're fine," he said quickly, and his friends nodded.

71
00:06:39.425 --> 00:06:49.204
Iphicles was already hurrying off. Brody and the others followed, not talking much until they'd walked for at least twenty minutes.

72
00:06:49.205 --> 00:06:55.424
Finally Heracles stopped his brother with a hand on the shoulder. "Let's rest here."

73
00:06:55.425 --> 00:07:02.244
Brody looked around. They were in a pleasant clearing with a babbling brook running through it.

74
00:07:02.245 --> 00:07:06.621
He walked over and splashed cool water on his face.

75
00:07:06.622 --> 00:07:16.035
The kids all sat down together. For a few moments, nobody seemed to know what to say. Brody felt awkward.

76
00:07:16.036 --> 00:07:21.529
Heracles was supposed to be his enemy, but he'd just saved Brody's life.

77
00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:27.451
Now what was Brody supposed to think of him?

